<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Muye</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1046 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Muye was fought around 1046 BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-wu-of-zhou">King Wu of Zhou</a> and his allies and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/di-xin">Di Xin</a>, the last king of the Shang dynasty. The Shang army was routed near their capital, and Di Xin killed himself. The victory established the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a> and was later justified as a transfer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandate-of-heaven">Mandate of Heaven</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-muye.jpg" alt="Battle of Muye" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Muye.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
